{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.PhiQAjMachineryIdentification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.PhiQAjMachineryIdentification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.phi_q_li2_q_unified_via_aj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.phi_q_li2_q_unified_via_aj","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L243-L250","doc":"**Corollary (unconditional)**: Φ_q and Li_2^q are two archimedean\nlenses on the one algebraic object Â_K — and the lenses are\ngenuinely different: no parameter lies in both regimes\n(`saddle_regimes_disjoint`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:phi-q-aj-machinery-identification","label":"prop:phi-q-aj-machinery-identification","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.li2_q_eq_aj_saddle_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.li2_q_eq_aj_saddle_real","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L230-L241","doc":"**Main theorem (conditional)**: under the AJ conjecture + the\nRogers-as-AJ-saddle identification, at every real parameter\n`q ∈ (0,1)` the Jones tower and the Li_2^q saddle tower lie in the\nsame solution space of Â_K. Derived, not projected. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.phi_q_eq_aj_saddle_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.phi_q_eq_aj_saddle_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L210-L228","doc":"**Main theorem (conditional)**: under the AJ conjecture + the\nFaddeev-as-AJ-saddle identification, at every root-of-unity\nparameter the Jones tower and the Φ_q saddle tower lie in the SAME\nsolution space of Â_K — every linear combination of the two is\nannihilated. Derived by composing the two class fields through the\nproved superposition principle (§3b-cond item 5: the classes carry\nthe hypotheses, the theorem derives). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator.saddle_annihilated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator.saddle_annihilated","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L205-L205","doc":"The identification: in the real regime the saddle tower is\nannihilated by the same Â_K. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator.saddleTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator.saddleTower","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L202-L202","doc":"The Li_2^q-generated leading-order saddle tower at parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L200-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Li2QRegulator","kind":"class","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L195-L206","doc":"**Class axiomatisation of the Li_2^q (Rogers) identification**: the\nsaddle tower generated by Li_2^q solves the same Â_K recursion in\nthe real regime `q ∈ (0, 1)`. The regime is an ordering condition,\nhence stated over `ℝ` (AGENTS.md §7c archimedean wall). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator.saddle_annihilated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator.saddle_annihilated","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L192-L192","doc":"The identification: in the root-of-unity regime the saddle tower\nis annihilated by the same Â_K. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator.saddleTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator.saddleTower","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L189-L189","doc":"The Φ_q-generated leading-order saddle tower at parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.PhiQRegulator","kind":"class","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L179-L193","doc":"**Class axiomatisation of the Φ_q (compact q-dilog) identification**: the\nsaddle tower generated by the framework's Φ_q regulator solves the\nSAME Â_K recursion in the root-of-unity regime (`q^N = 1`, `q ≠ 1`,\n`N ≥ 2`) — \"Φ_q is the AJ saddle at `q = e^{2πi/N}`\", stated at the\nalgebraic level (the asymptotic/analytic half of the saddle-point\nstatement is part of the open literature input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L177-L177","doc":"Â_K is not the zero operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.annihilates","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L175-L175","doc":"The annihilation `Â_K · J_N(K; q) = 0` (the AJ recursion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.jones","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L173-L173","doc":"The N-colored Jones tower of K, as a function of the parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.homogeneous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.homogeneous","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L171-L171","doc":"Â_K is homogeneous: `Â_K · J = 0`, no inhomogeneous term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.ahat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.ahat","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L169-L169","doc":"The annihilating operator Â_K. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial.mk","kind":"ctor","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L167-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QuantumAPolynomial","kind":"class","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L155-L177","doc":"**Class axiomatisation of the AJ conjecture (Garoufalidis 2004)**\nfor a knot complement K over the coefficient field F: a nontrivial\n*homogeneous* q-difference operator Â_K annihilates the N-colored\nJones tower at every invertible parameter.\n\nStatus: proved for 2-bridge knots (`le2006`), pretzel knots, many\nRolfsen-table cases. For 𝓑_3 specifically, VERIFIED OPEN: the link-AJ\nconjecture was only *formulated* in 2024 (`sawabe2024`, Hopf +\nWhitehead computed) and no Borromean recurrence ideal is published —\nsee docs/audits/2026-07-06-borromean-aj-literature-status.md.\nHence no instance here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.saddle_regimes_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.saddle_regimes_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L145-L151","doc":"**The two archimedean saddle regimes are genuinely disjoint**: a\nreal deformation parameter `q ∈ (0,1)` (the Li_2^q regime) is never\na root of unity (the Φ_q regime). Unconditional; replaces the\nformer string-label inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Annihilates.add_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Annihilates.add_smul","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L121-L143","doc":"**Superposition**: the solution space of a *homogeneous*\nq-difference operator at fixed `q` is closed under linear\ncombinations. This is the derivation engine for the two\nconditional theorems below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.qWeyl_commutation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.qWeyl_commutation","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L112-L119","doc":"**The q-Weyl relation `L̂ M̂ = q · M̂ L̂`** — the commutation relation\nof the algebra 𝒜_q in which Â_K lives (the .md's displayed\nrelation), proved on the function model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Lhat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Lhat","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L109-L110","doc":"The shift operator `L̂f(m) = f(q · m)` of the q-Weyl algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Mhat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Mhat","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The multiplication operator `M̂f(m) = m · f(m)` of the q-Weyl algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.NontrivialAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.NontrivialAt","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L99-L102","doc":"Non-triviality of `op` at `q`: the top coefficient is not\nidentically zero in `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.Annihilates","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L92-L97","doc":"`op` annihilates the tower `J` at deformation parameter `q`:\n`∑_j coeff_j(q, q^N) · J(N+j) = rhs(q, q^N)` for every color `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.rhs","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Inhomogeneous right-hand side, as a function of `(q, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.coeff","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Coefficient of the `j`-th shift, as a function of `(q, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.order","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The order (L̂-degree) of the operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.QDiffOperator","kind":"structure","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L80-L90","doc":"A q-difference operator acting on color towers — order (L̂-degree),\ncoefficient functions of `(q, m)`, and an inhomogeneous right-hand\nside (`0` for homogeneous). Local mirror of\n`QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight.QDifferenceOperator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.borromean","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L72-L76","doc":"The Borromean rings complement as a `KnotComplement`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement.volume","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Hyperbolic volume (in units of the Catalan constant for the\nBorromean case). Currently a placeholder; the genuine type would\nbe `ℝ` or an algebraic-over-`ℚ̄` number per the audit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement.num_cusps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement.num_cusps","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Number of cusps (= number of components of the link). For 𝓑_3,\nthis is 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PhiQAJMachineryIdentification.KnotComplement","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/phi-q-aj-machinery-identification.lean#L60-L70","doc":"Abstract knot complement parameter (a placeholder for the geometric\ndata of a hyperbolic 3-manifold with cusps). The framework's\nBorromean is the canonical instance. ","signatureChunk":0}]}